\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Immortal love, for ever full,
\par For ever flowing free,
\par For ever shared, for ever whole,
\par A never-ebbing sea:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Our outward lips confess the Name
\par All other names above,
\par Love only knoweth whence it came,
\par And comprehendeth love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. We may not climb the heavenly steeps
\par To bring the Lord Christ down:
\par In vain we search the lowest deeps,
\par For Him no depths can drown.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. In joy of inward peace, or sense
\par Of sorrow over sin,
\par He is His own best evidence,
\par His witness is within.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. For warm, sweet, tender, even yet
\par A present help is He;
\par And faith has still its Olivet,
\par And love its Galilee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. The healing of His seamless dress
\par Is by our beds of pain;
\par We touch Him in life's throng and press,
\par And we are whole again.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. Through Him the first fond prayers are said
\par Our lips of childhood frame,
\par The last now whispers of our dead
\par Are burdened with His name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. O Lord and Master of us all,
\par Whate'er our name or sign,
\par We own Thy sway, we hear Thy call,
\par We test our lives by Thine.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

